                        <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-2">Generative UI kills the App Store tax & ad models. They want walled gardens.</p>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Barrier 3 -->
                    <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded border border-stone-200">
                        <div class="text-stone-500 mb-2">
                            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M4 7v10c0 2.21 3.582 4 8 4s8-1.79 8-4V7M4 7c0 2.21 3.582 4 8 4s8-1.79 8-4M4 7c0-2.21 3.582-4 8-4s8 1.79 8 4m0 5c0 2.21-3.582 4-8 4s-8-1.79-8-4"></path></svg>
                        </div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-stone-700 text-sm">3. Empty Backend</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-2">Can't generate UI for fragmented protocols without synthetic data first.</p>
                    </div>
                    <!-- Barrier 4 -->
                    <div class="bg-white p-5 rounded border border-stone-200">
                        <div class="text-blue-500 mb-2">
                            <svg class="w-6 h-6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 6.253v13m0-13C10.832 5.477 9.246 5 7.5 5S4.168 5.477 3 6.253v13C4.168 18.477 5.754 18 7.5 18s3.332.477 4.5 1.253m0-13C13.168 5.477 14.754 5 16.5 5c1.747 0 3.332.477 4.5 1.253v13C19.832 18.477 18.247 18 16.5 18c-1.746 0-3.332.477-4.5 1.253"></path></svg>
                        </div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-stone-700 text-sm">4. Pedagogy vs Tech</h4>
                        <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 mt-2">Silicon Valley builds tools, not teachers. They underestimate cognitive load.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
             </div>
        </div>

        <!-- TAB: LAB STRATEGY -->
        <div id="tab-strategy" class="tab-content">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
                <!-- Proposal Card -->
                <div class="lg:col-span-2 bg-white rounded-lg p-8 rational-card">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-stone-800">The Pitch: Token Observatory Studio</h2>
                    <p class="text-stone-600 mb-6">
                        A rational lab to research, build, evangelize, and deploy Tokenized UI architecture.
                    </p>
                    
                    <div class="bg-stone-50 p-6 rounded-lg border border-stone-200 mb-6">
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-700 mb-3">Why a DPI-led Initiative?</h3>
                        <ul class="space-y-3">
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <span class="text-green-500 mr-2">✓</span>
                                <span class="text-sm text-stone-600"><strong>Strategic Void:</strong> Big Tech sells the destination (Ads). We need to build the map (Protocols).</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <span class="text-green-500 mr-2">✓</span>
                                <span class="text-sm text-stone-600"><strong>Timing:</strong> Technological Readiness is 85% (High). Protocol Maturity is 40% (Developing).</span>
                            </li>
                            <li class="flex items-start">
                                <span class="text-green-500 mr-2">✓</span>
                                <span class="text-sm text-stone-600"><strong>Public Good:</strong> Closed ecosystems won't solve for the next billion users.</span>
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>

                    <div class="mt-8">
                        <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-800 mb-2">Draft Email to Leadership</h3>
                        <div class="bg-white border border-stone-300 rounded p-4 text-sm font-serif text-stone-700 leading-relaxed shadow-inner">
                            <p class="mb-3"><strong>Subject:</strong> Proposal for Token Observatory Studio: Architecting the Probabilistic UI Layer</p>
                            <p class="mb-3">Team,</p>
                            <p class="mb-3">To effectively address the "Billion Users, Million Journeys" mission, we must evolve our UI architecture from the current canonical, pixel-deterministic model to an intelligent, probabilistic one. Rigid, hard-coded interfaces cannot scale to the vast cultural and literacy nuances of our target demographic. I am proposing a shift to a <strong>Tokenized UI Architecture</strong>, where UI elements are not merely design system components, but semantic assets infused with cultural, environmental, and literacy metadata.</p>
                            <p class="mb-3">This architecture introduces a <strong>Generative Layer</strong> between the user and the backend. Here, "Rhetorical Journeys"—personalized, context-aware navigational branches—are dynamically generated using these UI tokens. These journeys adapt to the user's intent and literacy level, effectively guiding them through the complexity, before converging back into the strict "Canonical Journey" required for the final transactional commit.</p>
                            <p class="mb-3">To make this viable and solve the "Liability Trap" that currently limits Big Tech to simple assistive models, we will implement a <strong>"Safe Harbor Simulation"</strong> (a "SimCity" state). This allows agentic UI workflows to be validated in a risk-free sandbox before affecting real-world data, effectively bridging the "Valley of Trust."</p>
                            <p>I propose establishing the <strong>Token Observatory Studio</strong> as a rational lab to research, build, and evangelize this protocol-first approach. Unlike Big Tech, which prioritizes its walled gardens, this initiative builds the open "Map" for the next generation of intelligent interfaces.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Readiness Gauge -->
                <div class="bg-white rounded-lg p-6 rational-card">
                    <h3 class="text-sm font-bold text-stone-500 uppercase tracking-wide mb-4">Readiness Analysis</h3>
                    <div class="space-y-6">
                        <div>
                            <div class="flex justify-between text-xs font-bold text-stone-700 mb-1">
                                <span>Tech Readiness</span>
                                <span>85%</span>
                            </div>
